        "title": "Applying the Quadratic Formula",
        "text": "For t² - 3t - 9 = 0, use t = (-b ± √(b² - 4ac))/2a with a=1, b=-3, c=-9. So t = (3 ± √(9+36))/2 = (3 ± √45)/2.",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "DBE NSC",
        "license": "Public Domain"
    },
    {
        "id": "vpm-002b-h3",
        "type": "hint",
